I like this option the best. I'm pretty sure that if you are fast and
he is not, and you move directly away from him, then he can't hit you.
The danger, of course, is that you will run into something else.
Therefore my advice is to carefully retrace your steps by one square
(assuming that puts you out of the priest's reach) and hope that no-one
else has moved into that square in the meantime. Repeat until you have
a square's distance between you and the priest. Use your next turn to
open your BoH.

Of course the worry is that even if you outrun him, he'll hit you with
a ranged attack, but unless it's a p[articularly nasty wand it's
unlikely to take 37 hit points. He might also try summoning insects,
which in your situation could either ruin your day completely or create
a handy buffer between you and the priest. Depends how much of a threat
those bugs will pose to your character.

The big question is, will an angered priest move out of his temple in
puruit, or will he just wait for the player to come back?

